<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>China keeps a close eye on US midterm shake-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f0d5f4200443b7c67768c4aed025985de2f4db2cf96d81eb0def9429872b9d2</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T15:03:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261106-china-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-shake-up" /><summary type="html">The US midterm elections have resulted in the Democratic Party taking control of both chambers of the US Congress, leaving Donald Trump as a lame duck president for the remainder of his term. Professor Steve Tsang of the SOAS China Institute tells FRANCE 24 that, while a weakened Trump could strengthen Beijing's negotiating position, the Chinese leadership is aware that Congress has relatively little sway over foreign policy and is keen to maintain warm personal ties between the two presidents.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Pollution, shortages, crime: Daily life in Pakistan's megacity Karachi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18fccd1a3eac7b12fa4a307a8aaf383ebf21ba076c9ceff0032e30720dcabc54</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261106-pollution-shortages-crime-daily-life-in-pakistan-s-megacity-karachi" /><summary type="html">Fed up with hours of power cuts, the residents of Pakistan's economic hub Karachi took to the streets in recent days and blocked several major roads. The outburst of anger highlights the daily problems faced by a megacity of over 21 million people, which has once again been ranked among the world's least liveable cities.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Civilians under fire from military junta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2788ca514ccb9c70f17467712eebedddedeb8e5c3c4ab470e71f579257d4598b</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:58:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta--4174803e3ee2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta" /><summary type="html">More than five years after the military coup, the junta launched a new offensive in September to retake Rakhine State, intensifying airstrikes against civilians and employing double-tap strikes</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist jailed for 10 more years for collusion with foreign forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd924a175261f7bea7615e4283527028b11aacb816fc5589758536028930f3e6</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:29:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-hong-kong-activist-jailed-for-10-more-years-for-collusion-with-foreign-forces--7a7e3bb3e8a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-hong-kong-activist-jailed-for-10-more-years-for-collusion-with-foreign-forces" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in jail on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, the second time he has been penalised under the city's national security law. Hong, 30, is one of the most globally recognised faces of Hong Kong's pro-democracy movement and has already spent almost six years behind bars. He is now not due for release until late 2036.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong gets 10 more years in jail for foreign collusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b6cc7a5ea2fa4db5e311bdb6ada920f7d6997c70b5d86c8d644149c08ab8445</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T03:31:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion--961948348fab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in prison on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, a court summary said. Wong, 30, pleaded guilty in September to seeking foreign sanctions against Hong Kong and China under Beijing’s national security law, having spent nearly six years imprisoned.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea to deploy military mission to keep Strait of Hormuz open</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c680873f5b5faa8505f259921fe4bddd401dc17eb28a781eadbfaee3778c02c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T02:17:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz--37e442fe8805.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">South Korea will deploy maritime patrol aircraft and an explosive ordnance disposal team near the Strait of Hormuz to help keep the waterway open, its defence ministry said Thursday. Seoul said it would protect commercial shipping and energy supplies while ruling out military intervention in the ongoing US-Iran war.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>How Chinese AI is censoring the controversy around Mbappé’s Chairman Mao comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89e120253047f248b6bfe4c5a94b005bba9d9db22bf4e694361a0cdf4f6a0eac</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments--925db7d6d62f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments" /><summary type="html">Footballer Kylian Mbappé sparked a wave of condemnation across China when he implied that Chinese leader Mao Zedong was a dictator. In China, information about this controversy is being censored by Chinese AI chatbots.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea pushes digital detox for young people addicted to screens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b213756683e2618f0ac05a4393f924fe07bed33c29f6a7b0185456af47c4c2d3</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:14:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261104-south-korea-pushes-digital-detox-for-young-people-addicted-to-screens--7a9ca277cb2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261104-south-korea-pushes-digital-detox-for-young-people-addicted-to-screens" /><summary type="html">Back in August, France's Constitutional Council overturned a social media ban for children under 15. Some students, though, are now banned from using their smartphones at school. In South Korea, where an estimated 40 percent of young children and teens are addicted to their mobile devices, authorities are trying to find ways to drastically reduce their screen time – a huge challenge in such a hyper-connected society. FRANCE 24's Chloé Borgnon, Aruna Popuri and Justin McCurry report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea rejects US allegations over $6 billion Binance crypto heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f380a835a343dbb7d08b2e454975c33cb0ff9ceb040b253cb89cdaeeb9886175</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T23:49:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-north-korea-rejects-us-allegations-over-6-billion-binance-crypto-heist--685d3b1c8c8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-north-korea-rejects-us-allegations-over-6-billion-binance-crypto-heist" /><summary type="html">North Korea on Tuesday dismissed US allegations that it was behind a $6 billion cryptocurrency theft from Binance as "absurd rhetoric", accusing Washington of seeking to portray the country as a cybercriminal state and warning that US hostility could affect future diplomatic engagement.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Football: China refuses to air Real Madrid game after Mbappé comment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d6ee70b85679b07e35eecc290608210a612f7385e4d71048720b06058b51f1c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:09:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-football-china-refuses-to-air-real-madrid-game-after-mbapp_-comment--ab89cdb57c26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-football-china-refuses-to-air-real-madrid-game-after-mbapp%C3%A9-comment" /><summary type="html">Chinese state broadcaster CCTV did not broadcast a Real Madrid La Liga match on Sunday after star forward Kylian Mbappé caused a furore in China with remarks he made about former leader Mao Zedong. FRANCE 24's correspondent Jan Camenzind Broomby reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Taliban voices 'serious concern' over US plan to deport Afghan migrants via Pakistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:379bb041e8f531c7501ac69ab2348ff6df351835ca10df40f9d19223c0d97eea</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:26:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-taliban-voice-alarm-over-us-plan-to-deport-afghan-migrants-via-pakistan--7e5b3b112799.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-taliban-voice-alarm-over-us-plan-to-deport-afghan-migrants-via-pakistan" /><summary type="html">Afghanistan's Taliban government expressed concern on Monday over reported US plans to deport more than 150 Afghans from the US to Pakistan for an eventual return home, with advocacy groups warning the removal could endanger their lives.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands join Indian opposition protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57da87b58fec04bcb98abc41ce142610082b75e9be529c444448949751035d1b</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T17:45:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-join-indian-opposition-protest--b6cc09af60fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-join-indian-opposition-protest" /><summary type="html">India’s opposition parties staged major protests in New Delhi on Sunday against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government and a nationwide voter list review that has fuelled demonstrations since the summer, led by the youth movement Cockroach Janta Party. Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indian opposition parties stage mega rally seeking election chief’s resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:632a2d06b585a10a438ee38bedc428f0c5c1789b4e48c6375edf2378c3fb22ef</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T06:24:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261101-india-tightens-security-as-opposition-holds-mega-rally-demanding-election-chief-s-resignati--cf6cc8f746e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261101-india-tightens-security-as-opposition-holds-mega-rally-demanding-election-chief-s-resignation" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of demonstrators on Sunday joined a protest in New Delhi called by Indian opposition leader Rahul Gandhi and backed by the youth “Cockroach” movement amid tight security. Protesters are demanding the resignation of the country's election chief over voter list revisions that critics say favour Prime Minister Narendra Modi's party.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey nominates former foreign minister Sinirlioglu as UN chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d01d2a7d7a71aaab471da5fd53728d23a1d1d6f812ee42a6174c44b5d4384772</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T14:28:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261031-turkey-nominates-former-foreign-minister-sinirlioglu-as-un-chief--8c6274edaf1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261031-turkey-nominates-former-foreign-minister-sinirlioglu-as-un-chief" /><summary type="html">Turkey has nominated its former foreign minister and UN ambassador Feridun Hadi Sinirlioglu for the position of UN secretary-general, state-media reported on Saturday. The submission was officially backed by Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan who has been particularly vocal in calling for reform of the UN Security Council.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Foiled Hindu temple plot exposes rising anti-Indian sentiment in the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71819415624cb66026e4d3ba54dc7111c178e964ad1787c0b401e2d474113706</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:02:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261030-foiled-hindu-temple-plot-exposes-rising-anti-indian-sentiment-in-the-us--a53aa309830f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261030-foiled-hindu-temple-plot-exposes-rising-anti-indian-sentiment-in-the-us" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Access Asia, we explore why anti-Indian sentiment is rising in the United States in the wake of the foiled plot targeting a Hindu temple in Illinois. We ask the executive director of the Center for the Study of Organized Hate what's behind the trend, and whether the rhetoric coming from the Trump White House is to blame.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea tests attack drones as Kim calls for 'absolute superiority'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcb1b0c9945e02b5aab554b01542a18a9e5446b832f66af9920b22045ac7825a</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T00:22:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261030-north-korea-tests-attack-drones-as-kim-calls-for-absolute-superiority--e838605aa02a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261030-north-korea-tests-attack-drones-as-kim-calls-for-absolute-superiority" /><summary type="html">North Korea has tested attack drones, cruise missiles and rocket launchers at a weapons demonstration, state media reported Friday, as Kim Jong Un called for faster development of military drone and artificial intelligence technology. The tests follow a series of weapons trials and rising tensions with South Korea.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Food safety in India: A challenge for the world's most populous country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c16629e42cdcca88429e05edf2f2fbe00fc73e3eb47fa17861237a4b43f28acb</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T15:15:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261029-food-safety-in-india-a-challenge-for-the-world-s-most-populous-country--d71fe213e3e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261029-food-safety-in-india-a-challenge-for-the-world-s-most-populous-country" /><summary type="html">India's food industry feeds more than a billion people every day. But ensuring that what reaches consumers is safe has become an increasingly difficult challenge. The country has witnessed a rise in cases of food adulteration, with sometimes fatal consequences. As concerns over adulteration and poor hygiene grow, questions are being raised about whether regulators can effectively oversee such a sprawling sector.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong leader apologises and housing minister resigns after fire investigation exposes failures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f802f2bcd25545f9b151f4c4e70c5e6a1cb7990d585a68102f4ddf4a6292f657</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:29:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hong-kong-leader-apologises-and-housing-minister-resigns-after-fire-investigation-exposes-f--adfda34a535a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hong-kong-leader-apologises-and-housing-minister-resigns-after-fire-investigation-exposes-failures" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong Chief Executive John Lee apologised on Thursday for a fire that ravaged residential tower blocks in Tai Po in November 2025, killing 168, injuring 79 and displacing thousands of others. Housing Secretary Winnie Ho resigned Wednesday for her department's failure to supervise the maintenance work. A three-month investigation into conduct will follow, alongside proposals to criminalise bid rigging in relation to the complex's US $38 million renovation contract.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hello Kitty firm apologises, cuts ties with Japanese spy show after China backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d7f60b21b5fb78c82389d318a93bca50c71d3b9acaceba5c8f1bc1692fb710b</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T09:04:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hello-kitty-firm-apologises-cuts-ties-with-japanese-spy-show-after-china-backlash--4fb6031dd3c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-hello-kitty-firm-apologises-cuts-ties-with-japanese-spy-show-after-china-backlash" /><summary type="html">Sanrio, the company behind the hugely successful Hello Kitty franchise, has apologised and ended its commercial tie-up with a Japanese TV drama after Chinese state media accused the show of "smearing China", sparking a social media backlash.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires 'around a dozen' ballistic missiles amid rising tensions with South Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0417b46b267d29de2a931138948a0a0dc46f3070c9145eaf5132a8e2f950a77a</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T05:04:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-north-korea-launches-around-a-dozen-ballistic-missiles-amid-rising-tensions-with-south-kore--b8fb6dd944c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261029-north-korea-launches-around-a-dozen-ballistic-missiles-amid-rising-tensions-with-south-korea" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired around a dozen short-range ballistic missiles off its east coast on Thursday, Seoul's defence ministry said. The North Korean capital Pyongyang has stepped up weapons tests in recent weeks despite South Korea's offer of military talks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India: Over 180,000 evacuated on east coast as massive cyclone hits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:218c9d0ccab2d6cd6e0fa68d589fb434f9e87ffd5952cd171b7593a429d48fd1</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-india-over-180-000-evacuated-on-east-coast-as-massive-cyclone-hits--19a5510d46e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-india-over-180-000-evacuated-on-east-coast-as-massive-cyclone-hits" /><summary type="html">A 125-kilometer-per-hour cyclone hit the southeastern coast of India on Wednesday, October 28, as authorities warned of localised flooding and the uprooting of power and communications poles. At least 180,000 people have been evacuated, while neighbouring Sri Lanka and Nepal have also issued weather warnings. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Real Madrid apologises to China over Mbappé's Mao Zedong comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00939544506c4b0111d702951fd1ca0f52e9c493a7376fe66362968eb2ed0dbf</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T06:00:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261028-real-madrid-apologise-to-china-over-mbapp_-s-mao-zedong-comments--25ef5f10dfe3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261028-real-madrid-apologise-to-china-over-mbapp%C3%A9-s-mao-zedong-comments" /><summary type="html">Real Madrid apologised to the Chinese people on Wednesday after star striker Kylian Mbappé sparked a furious backlash over comments referring to the founding leader of Communist China as a dictator. The club's apology came a day after Mbappé and Spain's La Liga football championship expressed regret over the remarks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>As China's Communist Party holds plenum, Xi's anti-corruption drive continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73be6151060fed92c4f47cab29fe935afdaeb2e439b42f04ffee01c2e41f7607</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues--b51be6c2b893.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, we try to figure out what happens behind the closed doors of the Chinese Communist Party's plenum meeting. At the heart of the discussions will be President Xi Jinping's firm grip on power. For analysis, we're joined by Jean-François Di Méglio from the Asia Centre think tank.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Azerbaijan: Rare protests over hijab ban in schools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3957ff864d6a545a01c554f82dbc81eb850a4f3c22694a8fc0c8778fc4b3bd8</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:16:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools--72dbcc5dfced.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools" /><summary type="html">In Azerbaijan, a new government ban on hijab in schools has provoked rare public protests. The ban prohibits clothing deemed "incompatible with the secular principles of general education". While it does not mention Islamic hijab, girls and teachers wearing hijab have been turned away from schools. The measure has sparked tensions in a country where 96% of the population is Muslim.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Typhoon Champi batters Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fbc97fee6bd22416e374dfd705ec4bf9e2437b443bcb8f95e95f456f4bcd942</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan--3f52c552700e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan" /><summary type="html">Typhoon Champi is heading towards China and Japan. Yesterday, it battered Taiwan with heavy rain and winds reaching up to 180 kilometres per hour. Across the island, 56,000 households are without power. Nicolas Chamontin and Ophelie Jacobson report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why do women in public life become targets?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0a07abb33f86b7dba91c7a01228caf42422e71d0d35a6ebce00fd315b0e615</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:58:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets--350d0cae4873.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets" /><summary type="html">A brutal targeted attack on an Australian female MP, who lost both her legs as a result, has reignited concerns over the rising levels of violence against women in public life. Also Cornell University is facing a no-confidence vote over its handling of an alleged gang rape in 2024. Annette Young speaks to Annie E. Clark, a survivor of campus sexual assault and Dr Sara Wilf of George Mason University about why institutions continue to struggle with sexual assault cases.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Singapore's longevity industry: The quest for eternal youth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef07c3950021401f893669aff5fc3cdacad73974e354558a6a2e33b70fd8b4de</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth--7654b61f92cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth" /><summary type="html">In Singapore, the quest for eternal youth is no longer just a billionaire's fantasy. It's becoming big business. High-tech clinics, longevity labs and specialist companies all promise the same thing: slowing down the ageing process. From continuous metabolic monitoring and genetic testing to supplements and oxygen therapy, every aspect of the body is measured and optimised.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan shuts down schools and businesses as Typhoon Champi approaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23bd2a28bdfa77c74974527d2dbf34223fb014f01207c66c195ac3213994b24f</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T03:00:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches--0f72f77296ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches" /><summary type="html">As Typhoon Champi approached Taiwan, most businesses and schools were closed across the island Friday and hundreds of flights were canceled in the region. Authorities reported at least one death and dozens of injuries and more than 1,200 people have evacuated their homes.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Strong earthquake strikes China’s remote Tibet region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:504b68486d2e350798c61f66973cf3845f96cf34743898e4956704628ec5182c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T21:09:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven--9ae8ceb17977.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven" /><summary type="html">At least 16 people have died and dozens more injured after a major earthquake measuring 7.0 on the Richter scale shook China’s remote Tibet region on Thursday, state media said. Hundreds of houses collapsed in the tremor.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Dalai Lama appointed by China 'is going to be a fake one', exiled former Tibetan leader says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d6e6b426fd4d8c5484f089d5bf20c20ed8ce57dd3dc17473015e21f163b9a4c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:22:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says--f8e9f1f22fcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, exiled former Tibetan leader Lobsang Sangay said any successor to the Dalai Lama appointed by China "is going to be a fake one". He also likened Beijing's ethnic unity law to "an ethnic erasure", said Tibetan concerns had been "downgraded a bit" in US-China talks and accused China of failing to warn of the deadly August floods on the Nepal-Tibet border.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry></feed>
